  "answer_core": "I wouldn’t grant Marcus 15% equity, a board seat, and a CTO title on Friday. Those are long‑term, hard‑to‑reverse commitments, and you still need evidence about whether this partnership strengthens the company or concentrates risk around him.\n\nUse Friday for a direct, structured conversation that lays out a real but staged path. Make clear you’re open to meaningful upside if he proves out the relationship, but that you need a short, defined window to test what actually happens when he steps into a central role: platform delivery, revenue relevance, team continuity and behavior, knowledge transfer, and whether he reinforces or destabilizes governance.\n\nAvoid turning the discussion into valuation math or instrument mechanics. The goal is not delay; it’s establishing proof. Signal seriousness, define the evaluation window and what success unlocks, and keep commitments proportional to demonstrated impact rather than hypothetical upside.",
